$ whycant -u root write /etc/resolv.conf

✗ root (uid 0) cannot write /etc/resolv.conf

  /                  drwxr-xr-x      root:root  ✓ traverse
  /etc               drwxr-xr-x      root:root  ✓ traverse
  /etc/resolv.conf   -rw-r--r-- [i]  root:root  ✗ write   ← blocked here

Why
  /etc/resolv.conf has the immutable attribute: it cannot be changed, renamed or deleted,
  not even by root.

Fixes (safest first)
  1. Remove the attribute (someone set this on purpose; find out why first):
       sudo chattr -i /etc/resolv.conf
